y cuts and deferral of all discretionary expenses.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/23/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q1-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"FSV 2020 Q1","e":"fsv","d":"2020-04-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"Scott alluded to the cost reduction and cash management initiatives we have undertaken in the face of COVID-19, and that includes a review of our capital expenditures.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/23/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q1-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"FSV 2020 Q2","e":"fsv","d":"2020-07-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"This more modest impact to the top line together with pre-emptive and aggressive cost reduction initiatives drove the Brands division to solid profitability in a challenging environment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/23/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q2-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"FSV 2020 Q2","e":"fsv","d":"2020-07-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"As to the margin outlook in conjunction with that, a lot of the cost savings that we realized should remain in place.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/23/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q2-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"FSV 2020 Q3","e":"fsv","d":"2020-10-28","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"In closing my prepared comments, we reiterate our outlook from the second quarter earnings call.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/28/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q3-2020-earnings-call/"},{"c":"FSV 2020 Q4","e":"fsv","d":"2021-02-09","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Scott Patterson","x":"In terms of the cost savings we talked about that, a lot of that coming back on as we reopened facilities as we brought some of our labor driven services back in place.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/09/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q4-2020-earnings-call/"},{"c":"FSV 2021 Q1","e":"fsv","d":"2021-04-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"The pickup we expect to get from continued strong home resale activity lapping the prior year, pandemic-driven falloff will be largely offset by the reinvestments we have made since last Q2, when we took aggressive cost cutting measures to counter the acute COVID-19 environment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/28/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q1-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"FSV 2021 Q2","e":"fsv","d":"2021-07-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"So our ability to pass that through directly does give us good cover.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/27/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q2-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"FSV 2021 Q2","e":"fsv","d":"2021-07-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"So it's not a direct pass through, but again, we keep a close eye on this.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/27/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q2-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"FSV 2021 Q2","e":"fsv","d":"2021-07-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"And second, the margin level reflects reinvestment, including headcount additions for growth by most of our brands relative to last year's Q2 when aggressive COVID-related cost cutting initiatives were incurred.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/27/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q2-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"FSV 2021 Q3","e":"fsv","d":"2021-10-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"We can recoup some of this through cost-plus contracts, but much of it will be subject to a lag in getting price increases through contract renewals.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/26/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q3-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"FSV 2021 Q3","e":"fsv","d":"2021-10-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"So, in terms of dealing with the non-pass through cost-plus components, we believe that we're going to capture some of that wage inflation back through price increases as contracts renew, and those can be one-year or multiyear contracts.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/26/firstservice-corporation-fsv-q3-2021-earnings-call/"},{"c":"FSV 2025 Q2","e":"fsv","d":"2025-07-24","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Scott Patterson","x":"I mean, the tariff uncertainty, I think the expectation that interest rates would start moving down, and that has not happened.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/07/24/firstservice-fsv-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"FSV 2025 Q2","e":"fsv","d":"2025-07-24","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Stephen MacLeod","x":"Is it more macro-driven, or is it just people getting people who are making these large investment decisions getting more comfortable with the tariff situation?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/07/24/firstservice-fsv-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"FSV 2026 Q1","e":"fsv","d":"2026-04-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jeremy Rakusin","x":"Once we get through that and once new construction, new development resumes its normal course, we think the competitive pressures in reroof will abate and we will get more pricing power.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/23/firstservice-fsv-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"FSV 2026 Q1","e":"fsv","d":"2026-04-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Stephen Sheldon","x":"Are there still a lot of levers to pull where there could be structural margin improvement over the medium term and a better backdrop with more pricing power?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/23/firstservice-fsv-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"FSV 2026 Q1","e":"fsv","d":"20